sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 74/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The script performs a direct quantitative comparison of the Bressloff retino-cortical map's analytical derivative dx/dr against the empirical human V1 linear magnification law M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg from Horton and Hoyt (1991) over 1-40 deg, reporting 6.78% RMS relative error, 30.0% max relative error, implied A and E2 constants, and 0-90 deg cortical extent. It also computes 2D radial and azimuthal FFT power-spectrum metrics (k*, ring sharpness, m2/m4/m6 harmonics) on the cortical sheets and transparently discloses the fig40 odd-hex degeneracy and Rule (2011) acceptance failures. Deduct 10 points because the headline 2.22e-16 calibration parity in verify_paper_calibration_parity is parity with another software implementation (MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants, explicitly marked 'not a digitized paper figure' in paper-calibration.json) rather than empirical data or digitized curves from Bressloff et al. (2001). Deduct 7 points because spectral_ring_metrics is evaluated only on the flat cortical torus and no morphometrics (such as radial ring spacing vs eccentricity or spiral pitch) are measured on the rendered retinal pullbacks or compared to psychophysical data. Deduct 5 points because verify_paper_calibration_parity checks only the 5 entries in stability_reports (10/11 checks passed) and ignores the 16 preset entries in paper-calibration.json['runs'], where 7 presets have status 'review' and 10 same-lattice-branch checks fail (including fig31_square_even). Deduct 4 points because the Rule (2011) Fig. 8 RMS beta error (0.154) is read verbatim from rule-2011-floquet.json rather than computed from simulated fields. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L133–L164: Analytical comparison of model cortical magnification against Horton & Hoyt (1991) over 1-40 deg eccentricity. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L133-L164>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L878–L938: 2D radial and azimuthal FFT spectral ring discriminator computed on cortical planforms. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L878-L938>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L943–L1041: Parity check comparing against paper-calibration.json['stability_reports'] while omitting the 16 entries in paper-calibration.json['runs']. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L943-L1041>; datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json L345–L412: Upstream run entry for fig31_square_even with status 'review' and failed same-lattice-branch checks omitted from the script's summary. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json#L345-L412>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): bressloff-v1-form-constants stability_reports parity, max |Δ| = 0.0 dimensionless (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c) [maximum absolute error across all 5 Bressloff (2001) stability_reports (q*, λ*, γ(0), γ(θ), η_hex) vs paper-calibration.json]; Mexican-hat lateral inhibition critical wavenumber q* (Bressloff 2001 Fig. 16) = 1.028 dimensionless wavenumber (reference >0.5 (finite Turing/Euclidean symmetry-breaking wavelength), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 Fig. 16) [maximizer of max(λ_even(q), λ_odd(q)) with lateral_inhibition = 0.27] — interior peak prominence = 0.1200; Gaussian-only negative control critical wavenumber q* (lateral_inhibition = 0) = 0.05 dimensionless wavenumber (reference 0.05, q_min boundary of [0.05, 3.0] grid (monotonically decaying dispersion, prominence = 0.0)) [maximizer of λ(q) when Mexican-hat surround inhibition is removed (lateral_inhibition = 0.0)] — interior peak prominence = 0.00e+00; Klüver Tunnel/Rings cortical planform spectral ring sharpness = 31.331 ratio (peak/median PSD) (reference >5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 7 / Klüver 1966 Tunnel form constant) [2D FFT radial power spectrum peak/median ratio at k* = 11 cycles]; Klüver Honeycomb/Hex linear cortical planform spectral ring wavenumber k* = 11.0 cycles / domain (reference 11 (q*/d_hyp = 11.27 cycles), Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 35 / Klüver 1966 Honeycomb form constant) [dominant radial FFT wavenumber of the linear 3-mode hexagonal eigenmode superposition (non-contoured, weak tanh); the rendered wavenumber is q*/d_hyp quantised to integer cycles on the 2πβ/ε torus] — contoured-rendering k* = 21 (power moves to the √3·k difference ring); FFT lattice class = hexagonal; Retino-cortical magnification vs Horton & Hoyt (1991), RMS relative error over 1-40 deg = 0.0678 dimensionless (reference 0 (perfect agreement); map-implied A = α/ε = 18.72 mm/deg, E2 = w0/ε = 1.71 deg vs 17.3, 0.75, Horton & Hoyt 1991 Arch. Ophthalmol. 109:816 (doi:10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030); datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) [RMS of (α/(w0+εr) − 17.3/(E+0.75)) / (17.3/(E+0.75)) over 157 eccentricities in [1, 40] deg] — max |rel err| = 0.300; fovea→90° extent 74.6 mm (model) vs 83.0 mm (H&H); Upstream fixture paper-expectation checks passed (paper-calibration.json) = 10.0 count (reference 11.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c, stability_reports[*].checks) [number of the fixture's own expected-vs-actual checks that pass, out of 11] — fig40_odd_hex_bifurcation/selected-pattern: expected triangle, actual honeycomb; Rule et al. (2011) Fig. 8 overlay domain-normalised RMS β error (diagnostic, no calibration claim) = 0.154 normalised wavenumber β (reference <= 0.10 acceptance threshold (NOT met), Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout 2011 PLoS Comput. Biol. 7:e1002158 Fig. 8 via upstream fixture) [rule-2011-floquet.json source_curve_comparison.domain_beta_mapping.rms_error] — acceptance_status = outside-threshold-diagnostic; calibration_claim_allowed = False." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

